# The modules the initrd's init loads, in this order, each after those it needs (images/guest/modules.sh):
# Hyper-V's own drivers, which the pinned kernel builds as modules. The bus every Hyper-V device is on;
# the SCSI controller the guest's three disks are on, with the transport class it needs; the sockets the
# agent's ports and the Plan 9 shares reach the host by, with the socket family they are a transport of;
# and the balloon, whose free page reporting gives the memory the guest frees back to Windows. Never
# hv_utils, whose time sync would set the guest's clock under the agent.
hv_vmbus
scsi_transport_fc
hv_storvsc
vsock
hv_sock
hv_balloon
